WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.694
Palm's last tablet

00:00:01.506 --> 00:00:02.390
lives again

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:03.818
Long before the

00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:04.372
iPhone

00:00:04.455 --> 00:00:05.480
the Palm Pilot

00:00:05.292 --> 00:00:06.200
was the gadget

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:07.155
everyone wanted

00:00:07.285 --> 00:00:08.464
and its webOS

00:00:08.346 --> 00:00:09.395
made the devices

00:00:09.207 --> 00:00:10.905
useful and responsive

00:00:11.422 --> 00:00:12.565
A community effort

00:00:12.377 --> 00:00:13.591
has now restored

00:00:13.403 --> 00:00:14.853
Palm's last device

00:00:14.688 --> 00:00:15.549
and brought its

00:00:15.361 --> 00:00:16.598
operating system to

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:17.530
other platforms

00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:18.627
keeping the old

00:00:18.438 --> 00:00:19.735
platform alive

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.472
This past summer

00:00:21.284 --> 00:00:22.793
brought webOS Community

00:00:22.605 --> 00:00:23.725
Edition three point

00:00:23.536 --> 00:00:23.984
one

00:00:24.197 --> 00:00:25.859
replacing HP's final

00:00:25.671 --> 00:00:26.897
system image with

00:00:26.709 --> 00:00:27.486
a bundle of

00:00:27.298 --> 00:00:28.512
community additions

00:00:28.324 --> 00:00:29.196
and fixes

00:00:29.718 --> 00:00:30.732
Full story on

00:00:30.543 --> 00:00:31.439
the dashboard
